# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor. Java hits
# this harder than most languages here: `this.x = y;` and `return "literal";`
# are extremely common shapes, so several otherwise-obvious anchors (the
# constructor body at 79, every `return` inside the switch cases) generate a
# query matching three nodes and are refused.
#
# The anchors also deliberately avoid bodies whose method carries an
# annotation. `modifiers` is a *child* of method_declaration, so an @Override
# method's node starts on the annotation line, and a breadcrumb — which renders
# the node's first source line — reads "@Override" instead of the signature.
# That is a codemark rendering limit the profile cannot express; see
# grammars/java/README.md.

# Inside a loop inside a static factory inside a class:
# class Invoice > of(double...) > for (double amount).
# `items.add(...)` is the only call in that loop body.
87

# Inside a lambda inside a method: class Invoice > discounted > amount -> {}.
# Proves a lambda_expression body is reachable — the landmark no sample can
# propose, since a Java lambda never wraps a declaration.
120

# A switch inside a method: class Invoice > describe > switch (state).
# tree-sitter-java parses a statement-position switch as a switch_expression;
# there is no switch_statement kind, which is why the profile labels
# switch_block rather than the name that reads naturally.
134

# Inside a try inside a method: class Invoice > settle > try.
146

# Inside a constructor inside a class nested in a class:
# class Invoice > class Draft > Draft(Invoice owner).
# The deepest chain here: proves class-in-class containment and that
# `constructor` works as a container, which the built-in Java profile omits.
157
